From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RiPetitor <ripetitor@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:38:37 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] clk: rockchip: rk3568: Add 31.5 MHz HDMI clock

WS-35-640 requests 640x480 at 75 Hz with a 31.5 MHz pixel clock.
Without this rate, HDMI rejects the mode with MODE_NOCLOCK.

Add the integer PLL setting tested on ELTAY RM66 with BB CM4.
24 MHz / 4 * 189 / (6 * 6) gives 31.5 MHz exactly.

Signed-off-by: RiPetitor <ripetitor@proton.me>
---
 drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-rk3568.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-rk3568.c b/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-rk3568.c
--- a/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-rk3568.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-rk3568.c
@@ -92,6 +92,7 @@
 	RK3036_PLL_RATE(74250000, 2, 99, 4, 4, 1, 0),
 	RK3036_PLL_RATE(51200000, 1, 64, 6, 5, 1, 0),
 	RK3036_PLL_RATE(33300000, 4, 111, 5, 4, 1, 0),
+	RK3036_PLL_RATE(31500000, 4, 189, 6, 6, 1, 0),
 	{ /* sentinel */ },
 };
 
